@@ -609,3 +609,106 @@ The optional `OpenMedSpeech` product provides a pinned Core ML English speech ad
 ## Thermal admission for multimodal work
 
 `MultimodalThermalSession` can gate a local operation against current Apple thermal state, queue age and measured latency. See [Apple session admission](multimodal/thermal-latency-gates.md#apple-session-admission) for the policy table, recovery behavior and value-free evidence.
+
+## Keychain-backed policy and bundle trust secrets
+
+Policy secrets, such as the surrogate or hash keys a de-identification policy
+uses, and portable-bundle trust material, such as verification public keys or
+pins, stay out of model bundles, caches and policy files. Code depends on the
+small `OpenMedSecretProvider` protocol and passes opaque
+`OpenMedSecretReference` values. `OpenMedKeychainSecretProvider` is the bundled
+Apple implementation. It mirrors the custody boundary of the Python
+[surrogate-key providers](security/surrogate-key-providers.md) and does not
+change any surrogate algorithm.
+
+```swift
+let configuration = try OpenMedKeychainConfiguration(
+    service: "org.example.openmed.secrets",
+    accessGroup: .applicationDefault,            // or .named("TEAMID.org.example.shared")
+    accessibility: .whenUnlockedThisDeviceOnly,  // the default
+    userAuthentication: .notRequired             // or .userPresence, .biometryCurrentSet, ...
+)
+let provider = OpenMedKeychainSecretProvider(configuration: configuration)
+let reference = try OpenMedSecretReference(purpose: .policySecret, label: "study-a.hash-key")
+
+// The caller supplies the bytes; the provider never generates a key.
+let stored = try provider.put(callerManagedKey, for: reference)  // version 1
+let key = try provider.get(reference, expectedVersion: stored.version)
+// Pass key.bytes straight to the local operation; never log, cache or export them.
+let rotated = try provider.rotate(reference, to: nextCallerManagedKey, expectedVersion: 1)
+```
+
+The configuration is explicit. The access group has no default, and only the
+`ThisDeviceOnly` accessibility classes are offered (`whenUnlockedThisDeviceOnly`,
+`whenPasscodeSetThisDeviceOnly`, `afterFirstUnlockThisDeviceOnly`). Every call
+sends `kSecAttrSynchronizable = false` and `kSecUseDataProtectionKeychain = true`,
+including on macOS, so items never sync through iCloud Keychain and never land in
+a legacy file keychain. A `userAuthentication` other than `notRequired` stores
+the item with a `SecAccessControl` built from the configured class and the
+matching `SecAccessControlCreateFlags`, instead of `kSecAttrAccessible`.
+
+A reference hashes its purpose and caller label with SHA-256 and does not keep
+the label. The Keychain account is `omk.secret.v1.<digest>`, and descriptions
+show only `ref:` plus 16 hexadecimal characters. References encode as
+`{"purpose", "digest"}`, so a portable policy can name a secret without holding
+it. Use configuration names as labels, never patient or user data.
+`OpenMedSecretValue` is not `Codable`, and its description, debug description
+and mirror report the reference fingerprint, version and byte count only.
+Receipts, metadata and protection reports are `Codable` and value-free.
+
+| Operation | Result |
+| --- | --- |
+| `put(_:for:)` | Stores version 1. An existing item fails with `secret_duplicate` and is not overwritten. |
+| `get(_:expectedVersion:)` | Returns the bytes. With an expected version, a different stored version fails with `secret_rotated` instead of returning it. |
+| `metadata(for:)` | Returns the version from attributes only, without reading the bytes. |
+| `rotate(_:to:expectedVersion:)` | Replaces the bytes only if the item is still at the expected version. |
+| `delete(_:)` | Returns `deleted` or `already_absent`. |
+| `protectionReport()` | States the configured protection and whether this device can provide it. |
+
+Rotation is a compare-and-swap: the update matches the metadata the provider
+just read, so a concurrent rotation makes it miss and the call fails with
+`secret_rotated` rather than overwriting. The Keychain keeps only the current
+version. Store earlier material under its own reference first if it must stay
+readable.
+
+Every failure is an `OpenMedSecretProviderError` with a fixed `secret_*` code
+and no secret bytes, labels, service or account strings, access groups or
+platform messages. There is no plaintext, cached or weaker-protection fallback:
+
+- `secret_missing`: no item exists for the reference.
+- `secret_locked`: the device is locked or the system did not allow interaction
+  (`errSecInteractionNotAllowed`).
+- `secret_invalidated`: the item's attributes are readable but its bytes are
+  not, for example when a `biometryCurrentSet` item no longer opens after an
+  enrollment change, or its stored metadata is malformed or names another
+  purpose. Some OS versions report an invalidated item as
+  `secret_authentication_failed` instead.
+- `secret_rotated`: the stored version is not the one the caller expected.
+- `secret_protection_mismatch`: the item's accessibility class, sync flag or
+  recorded user-authentication mode differs from the configuration.
+- `secret_unsupported`: a write needs a passcode or biometry the device cannot
+  provide now, or the platform rejects the configuration. The write is refused
+  before any `SecItem` call rather than stored with weaker protection.
+- `secret_missing_entitlement` / `secret_unavailable`: the process cannot use
+  the data-protection Keychain at all.
+- `secret_user_canceled`, `secret_authentication_failed`, `secret_duplicate`,
+  `secret_invalid_*` and `secret_unexpected_status` cover the remaining cases.
+
+`protectionReport()` probes `LocalAuthentication` without a prompt and reports
+`not_requested`, `available`, `passcode_not_set`, `biometry_not_available`,
+`biometry_not_enrolled`, `biometry_lockout`, `unsupported_platform` or
+`unknown`. Biometry is `unsupported_platform` on watchOS. The report always
+sets `secureHardwareClaimed` to `false`. The items are generic passwords
+protected by OS data protection, not Secure Enclave keys, and the adapter makes
+no claim that a secret is held in, or never leaves, secure hardware.
+
+Calls can block or show a system authentication prompt, so make them off the
+main thread. Tests inject `OpenMedKeychainItemClient`, which wraps
+`SecItemAdd`, `SecItemCopyMatching`, `SecItemUpdate` and `SecItemDelete`, and
+`OpenMedLocalAuthenticationProbe`. The package tests use an in-memory fake to
+cover missing, locked, invalidated, rotated, mismatched and unsupported items.
+Set `OPENMED_KEYCHAIN_INTEGRATION=1` to run the optional system-Keychain round
+trip. An unsigned `swift test` runner on macOS lacks the data-protection
+Keychain entitlement, so that test skips with `secret_missing_entitlement`
+there. Locked-device, biometry-enrollment and Secure Enclave behavior needs a
+physical device and is not covered by the package tests.
diff --git a/swift/OpenMedKit/Sources/OpenMedKit/KeychainSecretProvider.swift b/swift/OpenMedKit/Sources/OpenMedKit/KeychainSecretProvider.swift
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..b28c8db78
--- /dev/null
+++ b/swift/OpenMedKit/Sources/OpenMedKit/KeychainSecretProvider.swift
@@ -0,0 +1,585 @@
+import Foundation
+import Security
+
+#if canImport(LocalAuthentication)
+    import LocalAuthentication
+#endif
+
+/// The four `SecItem` calls the Keychain provider makes, so tests and hosts
+/// can substitute a fake or an instrumented store.
+///
+/// Query and attribute dictionaries use the `Security` framework keys. Add
+/// and update dictionaries carry secret bytes under `kSecValueData`, so an
+/// implementation must never log or persist them.
+public protocol OpenMedKeychainItemClient: Sendable {
+    /// Mirror `SecItemAdd` without returning a result.
+    func add(_ attributes: [String: Any]) -> OSStatus
+    /// Mirror `SecItemCopyMatching`.
+    func copyMatching(_ query: [String: Any]) -> (status: OSStatus, result: AnyObject?)
+    /// Mirror `SecItemUpdate`.
+    func update(_ query: [String: Any], attributes: [String: Any]) -> OSStatus
+    /// Mirror `SecItemDelete`.
+    func delete(_ query: [String: Any]) -> OSStatus
+}
+
+/// The system Keychain through `SecItemAdd`, `SecItemCopyMatching`,
+/// `SecItemUpdate` and `SecItemDelete`.
+public struct OpenMedSystemKeychainItemClient: OpenMedKeychainItemClient {
+    public init() {}
+
+    public func add(_ attributes: [String: Any]) -> OSStatus {
+        SecItemAdd(attributes as CFDictionary, nil)
+    }
+
+    public func copyMatching(_ query: [String: Any]) -> (status: OSStatus, result: AnyObject?) {
+        var result: CFTypeRef?
+        let status = SecItemCopyMatching(query as CFDictionary, &result)
+        return (status, result)
+    }
+
+    public func update(_ query: [String: Any], attributes: [String: Any]) -> OSStatus {
+        SecItemUpdate(query as CFDictionary, attributes as CFDictionary)
+    }
+
+    public func delete(_ query: [String: Any]) -> OSStatus {
+        SecItemDelete(query as CFDictionary)
+    }
+}
+
+/// A local-authentication capability a Keychain configuration depends on.
+public enum OpenMedLocalAuthenticationRequirement: String, CaseIterable, Sendable {
+    case devicePasscode = "device_passcode"
+    case biometry
+}
+
+/// Reports whether this device can currently evaluate a local-authentication
+/// requirement. Probing never shows a prompt.
+public protocol OpenMedLocalAuthenticationProbe: Sendable {
+    func availability(of requirement: OpenMedLocalAuthenticationRequirement) -> OpenMedProtectionAvailability
+}
+
+/// Probes `LocalAuthentication` with `LAContext.canEvaluatePolicy(_:error:)`.
+public struct OpenMedSystemLocalAuthenticationProbe: OpenMedLocalAuthenticationProbe {
+    public init() {}
+
+    public func availability(of requirement: OpenMedLocalAuthenticationRequirement) -> OpenMedProtectionAvailability {
+        #if canImport(LocalAuthentication)
+            let policy: LAPolicy
+            switch requirement {
+            case .devicePasscode:
+                policy = .deviceOwnerAuthentication
+            case .biometry:
+                #if os(watchOS)
+                    return .unsupportedPlatform
+                #else
+                    policy = .deviceOwnerAuthenticationWithBiometrics
+                #endif
+            }
+            var error: NSError?
+            if LAContext().canEvaluatePolicy(policy, error: &error) {
+                return .available
+            }
+            return Self.availability(forErrorCode: error?.code)
+        #else
+            return .unsupportedPlatform
+        #endif
+    }
+
+    /// Map a `LocalAuthentication` error code to an availability code.
+    static func availability(forErrorCode code: Int?) -> OpenMedProtectionAvailability {
+        #if canImport(LocalAuthentication)
+            switch code {
+            case Int(kLAErrorPasscodeNotSet):
+                return .passcodeNotSet
+            case Int(kLAErrorBiometryNotAvailable):
+                return .biometryNotAvailable
+            case Int(kLAErrorBiometryNotEnrolled):
+                return .biometryNotEnrolled
+            case Int(kLAErrorBiometryLockout):
+                return .biometryLockout
+            default:
+                return .unknown
+            }
+        #else
+            return .unsupportedPlatform
+        #endif
+    }
+}
+
+/// Explicit Keychain placement and protection for ``OpenMedKeychainSecretProvider``.
+///
+/// Every item is a generic password in the data-protection Keychain, bound
+/// to this device (`ThisDeviceOnly`) and never synchronizable. Descriptions
+/// and mirrors omit the service and access-group strings.
+public struct OpenMedKeychainConfiguration: Equatable, Sendable, CustomStringConvertible, CustomDebugStringConvertible, CustomReflectable {
+    /// When the system may decrypt an item. Only device-bound classes are offered.
+    public enum Accessibility: String, CaseIterable, Codable, Sendable {
+        /// `kSecAttrAccessibleWhenUnlockedThisDeviceOnly`; the default.
+        case whenUnlockedThisDeviceOnly = "when_unlocked_this_device_only"
+        /// `kSecAttrAccessibleWhenPasscodeSetThisDeviceOnly`; items are removed if the passcode is removed.
+        case whenPasscodeSetThisDeviceOnly = "when_passcode_set_this_device_only"
+        /// `kSecAttrAccessibleAfterFirstUnlockThisDeviceOnly`; readable while locked after the first unlock.
+        case afterFirstUnlockThisDeviceOnly = "after_first_unlock_this_device_only"
+
+        var constant: CFString {
+            switch self {
+            case .whenUnlockedThisDeviceOnly:
+                return kSecAttrAccessibleWhenUnlockedThisDeviceOnly
+            case .whenPasscodeSetThisDeviceOnly:
+                return kSecAttrAccessibleWhenPasscodeSetThisDeviceOnly
+            case .afterFirstUnlockThisDeviceOnly:
+                return kSecAttrAccessibleAfterFirstUnlockThisDeviceOnly
+            }
+        }
+    }
+
+    /// Which Keychain access group holds the items.
+    public enum AccessGroup: Equatable, Sendable {
+        /// The application's default group; no `kSecAttrAccessGroup` is sent.
+        case applicationDefault
+        /// A named group the app is entitled to, such as one shared with an extension.
+        case named(String)
+
+        var code: String {
+            switch self {
+            case .applicationDefault:
+                return "application_default"
+            case .named:
+                return "named"
+            }
+        }
+    }
+
+    /// The user authentication the system must see before releasing the bytes.
+    public enum UserAuthentication: String, CaseIterable, Codable, Sendable {
+        /// Only the accessibility class gates reads.
+        case notRequired = "not_required"
+        /// `SecAccessControlCreateFlags.userPresence`: biometry or the device passcode.
+        case userPresence = "user_presence"
+        /// `SecAccessControlCreateFlags.devicePasscode`.
+        case devicePasscode = "device_passcode"
+        /// `SecAccessControlCreateFlags.biometryAny`; survives enrollment changes.
+        case biometryAny = "biometry_any"
+        /// `SecAccessControlCreateFlags.biometryCurrentSet`; invalidated when enrollment changes.
+        case biometryCurrentSet = "biometry_current_set"
+
+        var flags: SecAccessControlCreateFlags? {
+            switch self {
+            case .notRequired:
+                return nil
+            case .userPresence:
+                return .userPresence
+            case .devicePasscode:
+                return .devicePasscode
+            case .biometryAny:
+                return .biometryAny
+            case .biometryCurrentSet:
+                return .biometryCurrentSet
+            }
+        }
+    }
+
+    /// The largest service or access-group string accepted, in UTF-8 bytes.
+    public static let maximumAttributeBytes = 256
+
+    /// The Keychain service namespace for this provider's items.
+    public let service: String
+    /// The access group holding the items.
+    public let accessGroup: AccessGroup
+    /// When the system may decrypt the items.
+    public let accessibility: Accessibility
+    /// The user authentication required to read the bytes.
+    public let userAuthentication: UserAuthentication
+
+    /// Always `true`: only `ThisDeviceOnly` accessibility classes are offered.
+    public var deviceOnly: Bool { true }
+    /// Always `false`: items never sync through iCloud Keychain.
+    public var synchronizable: Bool { false }
+
+    /// Create a configuration.
+    ///
+    /// - Parameters:
+    ///   - service: A non-blank namespace without control characters, at most
+    ///     ``maximumAttributeBytes`` UTF-8 bytes.
+    ///   - accessGroup: Where the items live; there is no implicit default.
+    ///   - accessibility: When the system may decrypt the items.
+    ///   - userAuthentication: The authentication required to read the bytes.
+    /// - Throws: ``OpenMedSecretProviderError/invalidConfiguration`` for an
+    ///   invalid service or access group.
+    public init(
+        service: String,
+        accessGroup: AccessGroup,
+        accessibility: Accessibility = .whenUnlockedThisDeviceOnly,
+        userAuthentication: UserAuthentication = .notRequired
+    ) throws {
+        guard Self.isValidAttribute(service) else {
+            throw OpenMedSecretProviderError.invalidConfiguration
+        }
+        if case .named(let group) = accessGroup, !Self.isValidAttribute(group) {
+            throw OpenMedSecretProviderError.invalidConfiguration
+        }
+        self.service = service
+        self.accessGroup = accessGroup
+        self.accessibility = accessibility
+        self.userAuthentication = userAuthentication
+    }
+
+    /// The local-authentication capabilities this configuration depends on.
+    public var requirements: [OpenMedLocalAuthenticationRequirement] {
+        var requirements: [OpenMedLocalAuthenticationRequirement] = []
+        switch (accessibility, userAuthentication) {
+        case (.whenPasscodeSetThisDeviceOnly, _), (_, .userPresence), (_, .devicePasscode):
+            requirements.append(.devicePasscode)
+        default:
+            break
+        }
+        if userAuthentication == .biometryAny || userAuthentication == .biometryCurrentSet {
+            requirements.append(.biometry)
+        }
+        return requirements
+    }
+
+    public var description: String {
+        "OpenMedKeychainConfiguration(\(accessibility.rawValue), access_group: \(accessGroup.code), user_authentication: \(userAuthentication.rawValue), synchronizable: false)"
+    }
+
+    public var debugDescription: String { description }
+
+    public var customMirror: Mirror {
+        Mirror(
+            self,
+            children: [
+                "accessibility": accessibility,
+                "accessGroup": accessGroup.code,
+                "userAuthentication": userAuthentication,
+            ],
+            displayStyle: .struct
+        )
+    }
+
+    private static func isValidAttribute(_ value: String) -> Bool {
+        let byteCount = value.utf8.count
+        guard byteCount > 0, byteCount <= maximumAttributeBytes else { return false }
+        guard !value.trimmingCharacters(in: .whitespacesAndNewlines).isEmpty else { return false }
+        return !value.unicodeScalars.contains { scalar in
+            scalar.properties.generalCategory == .control || CharacterSet.newlines.contains(scalar)
+        }
+    }
+}
+
+/// An ``OpenMedSecretProvider`` backed by the Apple data-protection Keychain.
+///
+/// Each reference maps to one generic-password item whose account is derived
+/// from the reference digest. The item's non-secret metadata (format, purpose,
+/// user-authentication code and version) lives in `kSecAttrGeneric`; the
+/// secret bytes live only in `kSecValueData`. The provider never generates a
+/// secret, never retains or caches bytes, never syncs, and never downgrades
+/// to weaker or plaintext storage when the Keychain refuses a call.
+public struct OpenMedKeychainSecretProvider: OpenMedSecretProvider, CustomStringConvertible, CustomDebugStringConvertible, CustomReflectable {
+    /// The largest secret accepted, in bytes.
+    public static let maximumSecretBytes = 16_384
+    /// The provider kind reported in ``OpenMedSecretProtectionReport``.
+    public static let providerName = "apple_keychain"
+
+    static let accountPrefix = "omk.secret.v1."
+
+    /// The placement and protection every item uses.
+    public let configuration: OpenMedKeychainConfiguration
+    private let client: any OpenMedKeychainItemClient
+    private let probe: any OpenMedLocalAuthenticationProbe
+
+    /// Create a provider.
+    ///
+    /// - Parameters:
+    ///   - configuration: Placement and protection for every item.
+    ///   - client: The `SecItem` calls; the system Keychain by default.
+    ///   - authenticationProbe: Checks passcode and biometry availability
+    ///     before a write; `LocalAuthentication` by default.
+    public init(
+        configuration: OpenMedKeychainConfiguration,
+        client: any OpenMedKeychainItemClient = OpenMedSystemKeychainItemClient(),
+        authenticationProbe: any OpenMedLocalAuthenticationProbe = OpenMedSystemLocalAuthenticationProbe()
+    ) {
+        self.configuration = configuration
+        self.client = client
+        self.probe = authenticationProbe
+    }
+
+    public func get(_ reference: OpenMedSecretReference, expectedVersion: Int?) throws -> OpenMedSecretValue {
+        if let expectedVersion, expectedVersion < 1 {
+            throw OpenMedSecretProviderError.invalidVersion
+        }
+        var query = itemQuery(for: reference)
+        query[kSecMatchLimit as String] = kSecMatchLimitOne
+        query[kSecReturnAttributes as String] = true
+        query[kSecReturnData as String] = true
+        let (status, result) = client.copyMatching(query)
+        switch status {
+        case errSecSuccess:
+            break
+        case errSecItemNotFound:
+            // The data read found nothing. If the attributes are still
+            // readable, the item exists but its access control no longer
+            // releases the bytes, for example after a biometry change.
+            _ = try attributes(for: reference)
+            throw OpenMedSecretProviderError.invalidated
+        default:
+            throw Self.error(for: status)
+        }
+        guard let attributes = result as? [String: Any],
+            let bytes = attributes[kSecValueData as String] as? Data
+        else {
+            throw OpenMedSecretProviderError.invalidated
+        }
+        let metadata = try validatedMetadata(attributes, for: reference)
+        if let expectedVersion, metadata.version != expectedVersion {
+            throw OpenMedSecretProviderError.rotated
+        }
+        guard Self.isAcceptedLength(bytes.count) else {
+            throw OpenMedSecretProviderError.invalidated
+        }
+        return OpenMedSecretValue(reference: reference, version: metadata.version, bytes: bytes)
+    }
+
+    public func metadata(for reference: OpenMedSecretReference) throws -> OpenMedSecretMetadata {
+        let metadata = try validatedMetadata(attributes(for: reference), for: reference)
+        return OpenMedSecretMetadata(reference: reference, version: metadata.version)
+    }
+
+    public func put(_ secret: Data, for reference: OpenMedSecretReference) throws -> OpenMedSecretReceipt {
+        guard Self.isAcceptedLength(secret.count) else {
+            throw OpenMedSecretProviderError.invalidSecret
+        }
+        try requireProtectionAvailable()
+        var attributes = itemQuery(for: reference)
+        attributes[kSecAttrGeneric as String] = KeychainSecretItemMetadata(purpose: reference.purpose, userAuthentication: configuration.userAuthentication, version: 1).encoded
+        attributes[kSecValueData as String] = secret
+        try applyProtection(to: &attributes)
+        let status = client.add(attributes)
+        guard status == errSecSuccess else {
+            throw Self.error(for: status)
+        }
+        return OpenMedSecretReceipt(operation: .stored, reference: reference, version: 1, byteCount: secret.count)
+    }
+
+    public func rotate(_ reference: OpenMedSecretReference, to secret: Data, expectedVersion: Int) throws -> OpenMedSecretReceipt {
+        guard Self.isAcceptedLength(secret.count) else {
+            throw OpenMedSecretProviderError.invalidSecret
+        }
+        guard expectedVersion >= 1, expectedVersion < Int.max else {
+            throw OpenMedSecretProviderError.invalidVersion
+        }
+        try requireProtectionAvailable()
+        let current = try validatedMetadata(attributes(for: reference), for: reference)
+        guard current.version == expectedVersion else {
+            throw OpenMedSecretProviderError.rotated
+        }
+        let next = KeychainSecretItemMetadata(purpose: reference.purpose, userAuthentication: configuration.userAuthentication, version: expectedVersion + 1)
+        // Matching on the stored metadata makes the update a compare-and-swap:
+        // a concurrent rotation changes kSecAttrGeneric and the update misses.
+        var query = itemQuery(for: reference)
+        query[kSecAttrGeneric as String] = current.encoded
+        let changes: [String: Any] = [
+            kSecValueData as String: secret,
+            kSecAttrGeneric as String: next.encoded,
+        ]
+        let status = client.update(query, attributes: changes)
+        switch status {
+        case errSecSuccess:
+            return OpenMedSecretReceipt(operation: .rotated, reference: reference, version: next.version, byteCount: secret.count)
+        case errSecItemNotFound:
+            _ = try attributes(for: reference)
+            throw OpenMedSecretProviderError.rotated
+        default:
+            throw Self.error(for: status)
+        }
+    }
+
+    public func delete(_ reference: OpenMedSecretReference) throws -> OpenMedSecretDeletion {
+        let status = client.delete(itemQuery(for: reference))
+        switch status {
+        case errSecSuccess:
+            return .deleted
+        case errSecItemNotFound:
+            return .alreadyAbsent
+        default:
+            throw Self.error(for: status)
+        }
+    }
+
+    public func protectionReport() -> OpenMedSecretProtectionReport {
+        OpenMedSecretProtectionReport(
+            provider: Self.providerName,
+            accessibility: configuration.accessibility.rawValue,
+            userAuthentication: configuration.userAuthentication.rawValue,
+            accessGroup: configuration.accessGroup.code,
+            deviceOnly: configuration.deviceOnly,
+            synchronizable: configuration.synchronizable,
+            availability: availability(),
+            secureHardwareClaimed: false
+        )
+    }
+
+    public var description: String {
+        "OpenMedKeychainSecretProvider(\(configuration.description))"
+    }
+
+    public var debugDescription: String { description }
+
+    public var customMirror: Mirror {
+        Mirror(self, children: ["configuration": configuration], displayStyle: .struct)
+    }
+
+    /// Map a `Security` status to a value-free error code.
+    static func error(for status: OSStatus) -> OpenMedSecretProviderError {
+        switch status {
+        case errSecItemNotFound:
+            return .missing
+        case errSecDuplicateItem:
+            return .duplicate
+        case errSecInteractionNotAllowed:
+            return .locked
+        case errSecUserCanceled:
+            return .userCanceled
+        case errSecAuthFailed:
+            return .authenticationFailed
+        case errSecMissingEntitlement:
+            return .missingEntitlement
+        case errSecNotAvailable:
+            return .unavailable
+        case errSecUnimplemented, errSecParam:
+            return .unsupported
+        default:
+            return .unexpectedStatus
+        }
+    }
+
+    /// The account an item is stored under; derived from the digest only.
+    static func account(for reference: OpenMedSecretReference) -> String {
+        accountPrefix + reference.digest
+    }
+
+    func itemQuery(for reference: OpenMedSecretReference) -> [String: Any] {
+        var query: [String: Any] = [
+            kSecClass as String: kSecClassGenericPassword,
+            kSecAttrService as String: configuration.service,
+            kSecAttrAccount as String: Self.account(for: reference),
+            kSecAttrSynchronizable as String: false,
+            kSecUseDataProtectionKeychain as String: true,
+        ]
+        if case .named(let group) = configuration.accessGroup {
+            query[kSecAttrAccessGroup as String] = group
+        }
+        return query
+    }
+
+    func availability() -> OpenMedProtectionAvailability {
+        let requirements = configuration.requirements
+        guard !requirements.isEmpty else { return .notRequested }
+        for requirement in requirements {
+            let availability = probe.availability(of: requirement)
+            if availability != .available {
+                return availability
+            }
+        }
+        return .available
+    }
+
+    private func requireProtectionAvailable() throws {
+        switch availability() {
+        case .notRequested, .available:
+            return
+        case .biometryLockout:
+            throw OpenMedSecretProviderError.authenticationFailed
+        case .passcodeNotSet, .biometryNotAvailable, .biometryNotEnrolled, .unsupportedPlatform, .unknown:
+            throw OpenMedSecretProviderError.unsupported
+        }
+    }
+
+    private func applyProtection(to attributes: inout [String: Any]) throws {
+        guard let flags = configuration.userAuthentication.flags else {
+            attributes[kSecAttrAccessible as String] = configuration.accessibility.constant
+            return
+        }
+        var error: Unmanaged<CFError>?
+        guard let accessControl = SecAccessControlCreateWithFlags(nil, configuration.accessibility.constant, flags, &error) else {
+            error?.release()
+            throw OpenMedSecretProviderError.unsupported
+        }
+        attributes[kSecAttrAccessControl as String] = accessControl
+    }
+
+    private func attributes(for reference: OpenMedSecretReference) throws -> [String: Any] {
+        var query = itemQuery(for: reference)
+        query[kSecMatchLimit as String] = kSecMatchLimitOne
+        query[kSecReturnAttributes as String] = true
+        let (status, result) = client.copyMatching(query)
+        guard status == errSecSuccess else {
+            throw Self.error(for: status)
+        }
+        guard let attributes = result as? [String: Any] else {
+            throw OpenMedSecretProviderError.invalidated
+        }
+        return attributes
+    }
+
+    private func validatedMetadata(_ attributes: [String: Any], for reference: OpenMedSecretReference) throws -> KeychainSecretItemMetadata {
+        if let synchronizable = attributes[kSecAttrSynchronizable as String] as? Bool, synchronizable {
+            throw OpenMedSecretProviderError.protectionMismatch
+        }
+        if let accessible = attributes[kSecAttrAccessible as String] as? String,
+            accessible != configuration.accessibility.constant as String
+        {
+            throw OpenMedSecretProviderError.protectionMismatch
+        }
+        guard let encoded = attributes[kSecAttrGeneric as String] as? Data,
+            let metadata = KeychainSecretItemMetadata(encoded),
+            metadata.purpose == reference.purpose
+        else {
+            throw OpenMedSecretProviderError.invalidated
+        }
+        guard metadata.userAuthentication == configuration.userAuthentication else {
+            throw OpenMedSecretProviderError.protectionMismatch
+        }
+        return metadata
+    }
+
+    private static func isAcceptedLength(_ count: Int) -> Bool {
+        count > 0 && count <= maximumSecretBytes
+    }
+}
+
+/// The non-secret record stored in `kSecAttrGeneric`.
+struct KeychainSecretItemMetadata: Equatable {
+    static let format = "openmed.secret.v1"
+
+    let purpose: OpenMedSecretPurpose
+    let userAuthentication: OpenMedKeychainConfiguration.UserAuthentication
+    let version: Int
+
+    init(purpose: OpenMedSecretPurpose, userAuthentication: OpenMedKeychainConfiguration.UserAuthentication, version: Int) {
+        self.purpose = purpose
+        self.userAuthentication = userAuthentication
+        self.version = version
+    }
+
+    /// Parse the canonical encoding only; anything else is rejected.
+    init?(_ data: Data) {
+        guard data.count <= 256, let text = String(data: data, encoding: .utf8) else { return nil }
+        let fields = text.split(separator: ";", omittingEmptySubsequences: false)
+        guard fields.count == 4, fields[0] == Self.format,
+            fields[1].hasPrefix("purpose="), fields[2].hasPrefix("auth="), fields[3].hasPrefix("version="),
+            let purpose = OpenMedSecretPurpose(rawValue: String(fields[1].dropFirst("purpose=".count))),
+            let userAuthentication = OpenMedKeychainConfiguration.UserAuthentication(rawValue: String(fields[2].dropFirst("auth=".count))),
+            let version = Int(fields[3].dropFirst("version=".count)), version >= 1
+        else {
+            return nil
+        }
+        self.init(purpose: purpose, userAuthentication: userAuthentication, version: version)
+        guard encoded == data else { return nil }
+    }
+
+    var encoded: Data {
+        Data("\(Self.format);purpose=\(purpose.rawValue);auth=\(userAuthentication.rawValue);version=\(version)".utf8)
+    }
+}
diff --git a/swift/OpenMedKit/Sources/OpenMedKit/SecretProvider.swift b/swift/OpenMedKit/Sources/OpenMedKit/SecretProvider.swift
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..efc64fec9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/swift/OpenMedKit/Sources/OpenMedKit/SecretProvider.swift
@@ -0,0 +1,348 @@
+import CryptoKit
+import Foundation
+
+/// What a provider-held secret is used for.
+///
+/// The purpose is folded into the opaque reference, so one caller label under
+/// two purposes names two separate items.
+public enum OpenMedSecretPurpose: String, CaseIterable, Codable, Sendable {
+    /// Key material a de-identification policy uses, such as a surrogate or hash key.
+    case policySecret = "policy_secret"
+    /// Verification material for portable bundles, such as a public key or a pin set.
+    case bundleTrustAnchor = "bundle_trust_anchor"
+}
+
+/// Value-free failures from a secret provider.
+///
+/// Each case is a fixed code. No case carries, and no description repeats,
+/// secret bytes, caller labels, Keychain service or account strings, access
+/// groups, paths or raw platform messages.
+public enum OpenMedSecretProviderError: String, Error, LocalizedError, CaseIterable, Sendable {
+    /// The caller label or opaque digest is not a valid reference.
+    case invalidReference = "secret_invalid_reference"
+    /// The secret is empty or larger than the provider accepts.
+    case invalidSecret = "secret_invalid_value"
+    /// An expected version is not a positive integer, or the next version would overflow.
+    case invalidVersion = "secret_invalid_version"
+    /// The provider configuration is incomplete or malformed.
+    case invalidConfiguration = "secret_invalid_configuration"
+    /// No item exists for the reference.
+    case missing = "secret_missing"
+    /// An item already exists; rotate it instead of storing it again.
+    case duplicate = "secret_duplicate"
+    /// The device is locked, or the system did not allow user interaction.
+    case locked = "secret_locked"
+    /// The user dismissed the authentication prompt.
+    case userCanceled = "secret_user_canceled"
+    /// Authentication failed or is locked out.
+    case authenticationFailed = "secret_authentication_failed"
+    /// The item exists but can no longer be read, or its stored metadata is not trustworthy.
+    case invalidated = "secret_invalidated"
+    /// The item is at a different version than the caller expected.
+    case rotated = "secret_rotated"
+    /// The stored item's protection does not match the configured protection.
+    case protectionMismatch = "secret_protection_mismatch"
+    /// The configured protection is not available on this device or OS.
+    case unsupported = "secret_unsupported"
+    /// The process lacks the Keychain entitlement the configuration needs.
+    case missingEntitlement = "secret_missing_entitlement"
+    /// No Keychain is available to the process.
+    case unavailable = "secret_unavailable"
+    /// The platform returned a status this adapter does not classify.
+    case unexpectedStatus = "secret_unexpected_status"
+
+    public var errorDescription: String? { rawValue }
+}
+
+/// An opaque, caller-managed handle for one provider-held secret.
+///
+/// The caller label is hashed with the purpose and is not retained, so the
+/// reference, its storage name and every rendering of it carry only a
+/// SHA-256 digest. Use labels that are application configuration names, never
+/// patient or user data.
+public struct OpenMedSecretReference: Hashable, Sendable, Codable, CustomStringConvertible, CustomDebugStringConvertible, CustomReflectable {
+    /// The largest caller label accepted, in UTF-8 bytes.
+    public static let maximumLabelBytes = 256
+
+    private static let domain = "openmed.secret-reference.v1"
+
+    /// What the referenced secret is used for.
+    public let purpose: OpenMedSecretPurpose
+    /// Lowercase hexadecimal SHA-256 digest of the purpose and caller label.
+    public let digest: String
+
+    /// Create a reference from a caller label.
+    ///
+    /// - Parameters:
+    ///   - purpose: What the secret is used for.
+    ///   - label: A non-blank application label without control characters,
+    ///     at most ``maximumLabelBytes`` UTF-8 bytes. It is not retained.
+    /// - Throws: ``OpenMedSecretProviderError/invalidReference`` for an invalid label.
+    public init(purpose: OpenMedSecretPurpose, label: String) throws {
+        guard Self.isValidLabel(label) else {
+            throw OpenMedSecretProviderError.invalidReference
+        }
+        var hash = SHA256()
+        hash.update(data: Data(Self.domain.utf8))
+        for part in [purpose.rawValue, label] {
+            hash.update(data: Data([0]))
+            hash.update(data: Data(part.utf8))
+        }
+        self.purpose = purpose
+        self.digest = hash.finalize().map { String(format: "%02x", $0) }.joined()
+    }
+
+    /// Recreate a reference from a digest a provider or policy file recorded.
+    ///
+    /// - Throws: ``OpenMedSecretProviderError/invalidReference`` unless the
+    ///   digest is 64 lowercase hexadecimal characters.
+    public init(purpose: OpenMedSecretPurpose, digest: String) throws {
+        guard digest.utf8.count == 64, digest.utf8.allSatisfy(Self.isLowercaseHex) else {
+            throw OpenMedSecretProviderError.invalidReference
+        }
+        self.purpose = purpose
+        self.digest = digest
+    }
+
+    private enum CodingKeys: String, CodingKey {
+        case purpose
+        case digest
+    }
+
+    public init(from decoder: Decoder) throws {
+        let container = try decoder.container(keyedBy: CodingKeys.self)
+        try self.init(
+            purpose: container.decode(OpenMedSecretPurpose.self, forKey: .purpose),
+            digest: container.decode(String.self, forKey: .digest)
+        )
+    }
+
+    /// A short, non-reversible handle for logs, receipts and diagnostics.
+    public var fingerprint: String { "ref:" + digest.prefix(16) }
+
+    public var description: String {
+        "OpenMedSecretReference(\(purpose.rawValue), \(fingerprint))"
+    }
+
+    public var debugDescription: String { description }
+
+    public var customMirror: Mirror {
+        Mirror(self, children: ["purpose": purpose, "fingerprint": fingerprint], displayStyle: .struct)
+    }
+
+    private static func isValidLabel(_ label: String) -> Bool {
+        let byteCount = label.utf8.count
+        guard byteCount > 0, byteCount <= maximumLabelBytes else { return false }
+        guard !label.trimmingCharacters(in: .whitespacesAndNewlines).isEmpty else { return false }
+        return !label.unicodeScalars.contains { scalar in
+            scalar.properties.generalCategory == .control || CharacterSet.newlines.contains(scalar)
+        }
+    }
+
+    private static func isLowercaseHex(_ byte: UInt8) -> Bool {
+        (UInt8(ascii: "0")...UInt8(ascii: "9")).contains(byte) || (UInt8(ascii: "a")...UInt8(ascii: "f")).contains(byte)
+    }
+}
+
+/// Non-secret state of one stored secret.
+public struct OpenMedSecretMetadata: Equatable, Sendable, Codable, CustomStringConvertible {
+    /// The opaque reference the item is stored under.
+    public let reference: OpenMedSecretReference
+    /// The current version; stores start at 1 and each rotation adds 1.
+    public let version: Int
+
+    /// Create metadata for a provider result.
+    public init(reference: OpenMedSecretReference, version: Int) {
+        self.reference = reference
+        self.version = version
+    }
+
+    public var description: String {
+        "OpenMedSecretMetadata(\(reference.purpose.rawValue), \(reference.fingerprint), version: \(version))"
+    }
+}
+
+/// A secret read from a provider.
+///
+/// Descriptions, debug descriptions and mirrors report the reference
+/// fingerprint, version and byte count only. The type is not `Codable` so it
+/// cannot be exported by accident.
+public struct OpenMedSecretValue: Sendable, CustomStringConvertible, CustomDebugStringConvertible, CustomReflectable {
+    /// The opaque reference the secret was read from.
+    public let reference: OpenMedSecretReference
+    /// The version that was read.
+    public let version: Int
+    /// The secret bytes. Pass them straight to the local operation that needs
+    /// them; never log, cache, persist or export them.
+    public let bytes: Data
+
+    /// Create a value for a provider result.
+    public init(reference: OpenMedSecretReference, version: Int, bytes: Data) {
+        self.reference = reference
+        self.version = version
+        self.bytes = bytes
+    }
+
+    /// The number of secret bytes.
+    public var byteCount: Int { bytes.count }
+
+    /// The value's non-secret metadata.
+    public var metadata: OpenMedSecretMetadata {
+        OpenMedSecretMetadata(reference: reference, version: version)
+    }
+
+    public var description: String {
+        "OpenMedSecretValue(\(reference.purpose.rawValue), \(reference.fingerprint), version: \(version), \(bytes.count) bytes)"
+    }
+
+    public var debugDescription: String { description }
+
+    public var customMirror: Mirror {
+        Mirror(self, children: ["reference": reference, "version": version, "byteCount": bytes.count], displayStyle: .struct)
+    }
+}
+
+/// A value-free record of a store or rotation, suitable for export.
+public struct OpenMedSecretReceipt: Equatable, Sendable, Codable, CustomStringConvertible {
+    /// The operation a receipt records.
+    public enum Operation: String, Codable, Sendable {
+        case stored
+        case rotated
+    }
+
+    /// The operation performed.
+    public let operation: Operation
+    /// The opaque reference written.
+    public let reference: OpenMedSecretReference
+    /// The version now stored.
+    public let version: Int
+    /// The number of secret bytes written.
+    public let byteCount: Int
+
+    /// Create a receipt for a provider result.
+    public init(operation: Operation, reference: OpenMedSecretReference, version: Int, byteCount: Int) {
+        self.operation = operation
+        self.reference = reference
+        self.version = version
+        self.byteCount = byteCount
+    }
+
+    public var description: String {
+        "OpenMedSecretReceipt(\(operation.rawValue), \(reference.purpose.rawValue), \(reference.fingerprint), version: \(version), \(byteCount) bytes)"
+    }
+}
+
+/// The outcome of deleting a reference.
+public enum OpenMedSecretDeletion: String, Codable, Sendable {
+    case deleted
+    case alreadyAbsent = "already_absent"
+}
+
+/// Whether this device can currently satisfy a provider's configured
+/// passcode and user-authentication requirements.
+public enum OpenMedProtectionAvailability: String, CaseIterable, Codable, Sendable {
+    /// The configuration requires no passcode or user authentication.
+    case notRequested = "not_requested"
+    /// Every configured requirement can be evaluated now.
+    case available
+    /// A required device passcode is not set.
+    case passcodeNotSet = "passcode_not_set"
+    /// Biometry is required but the device has none, or it is disabled.
+    case biometryNotAvailable = "biometry_not_available"
+    /// Biometry is required but nothing is enrolled.
+    case biometryNotEnrolled = "biometry_not_enrolled"
+    /// Biometry is required but locked out after failed attempts.
+    case biometryLockout = "biometry_lockout"
+    /// The platform cannot provide the required protection.
+    case unsupportedPlatform = "unsupported_platform"
+    /// The platform did not say why the requirement cannot be evaluated.
+    case unknown
+}
+
+/// Value-free description of the protection a provider requests and can get.
+///
+/// The report states configuration and probe results only. It makes no claim
+/// that a secret is held in, or never leaves, secure hardware.
+public struct OpenMedSecretProtectionReport: Equatable, Sendable, Codable, CustomStringConvertible {
+    /// The provider kind, such as `apple_keychain`.
+    public let provider: String
+    /// The configured accessibility class code.
+    public let accessibility: String
+    /// The configured user-authentication code.
+    public let userAuthentication: String
+    /// `application_default` or `named`; the group itself is never reported.
+    public let accessGroup: String
+    /// Whether items stay on this device and are not restored to another device from a backup.
+    public let deviceOnly: Bool
+    /// Whether items sync through a cloud keychain.
+    public let synchronizable: Bool
+    /// Whether this device can currently satisfy the configured requirements.
+    public let availability: OpenMedProtectionAvailability
+    /// Whether the provider claims secure-hardware custody of the secret bytes.
+    public let secureHardwareClaimed: Bool
+
+    /// Create a report for a provider.
+    public init(
+        provider: String,
+        accessibility: String,
+        userAuthentication: String,
+        accessGroup: String,
+        deviceOnly: Bool,
+        synchronizable: Bool,
+        availability: OpenMedProtectionAvailability,
+        secureHardwareClaimed: Bool
+    ) {
+        self.provider = provider
+        self.accessibility = accessibility
+        self.userAuthentication = userAuthentication
+        self.accessGroup = accessGroup
+        self.deviceOnly = deviceOnly
+        self.synchronizable = synchronizable
+        self.availability = availability
+        self.secureHardwareClaimed = secureHardwareClaimed
+    }
+
+    public var description: String {
+        "OpenMedSecretProtectionReport(\(provider), \(accessibility), user_authentication: \(userAuthentication), access_group: \(accessGroup), device_only: \(deviceOnly), synchronizable: \(synchronizable), availability: \(availability.rawValue), secure_hardware_claimed: \(secureHardwareClaimed))"
+    }
+}
+
+/// A small, injectable custody boundary for policy secrets and bundle trust
+/// material, addressed by opaque reference.
+///
+/// Providers never create secrets for the caller, never fall back to weaker
+/// or plaintext storage, and report every failure as an
+/// ``OpenMedSecretProviderError``. Calls may block or show a system
+/// authentication prompt, so call them off the main thread.
+public protocol OpenMedSecretProvider: Sendable {
+    /// Read the current secret.
+    ///
+    /// - Parameters:
+    ///   - reference: The opaque reference to read.
+    ///   - expectedVersion: When set, fail with
+    ///     ``OpenMedSecretProviderError/rotated`` unless the stored version
+    ///     matches, instead of returning a different version.
+    func get(_ reference: OpenMedSecretReference, expectedVersion: Int?) throws -> OpenMedSecretValue
+
+    /// Read the current version without reading or authenticating the secret bytes.
+    func metadata(for reference: OpenMedSecretReference) throws -> OpenMedSecretMetadata
+
+    /// Store a caller-supplied secret as version 1. Never overwrites an existing item.
+    func put(_ secret: Data, for reference: OpenMedSecretReference) throws -> OpenMedSecretReceipt
+
+    /// Replace the secret, only if it is still at `expectedVersion`.
+    func rotate(_ reference: OpenMedSecretReference, to secret: Data, expectedVersion: Int) throws -> OpenMedSecretReceipt
+
+    /// Delete the item. Deleting an absent item is not an error.
+    func delete(_ reference: OpenMedSecretReference) throws -> OpenMedSecretDeletion
+
+    /// Describe the configured protection and whether this device can provide it.
+    func protectionReport() -> OpenMedSecretProtectionReport
+}
+
+extension OpenMedSecretProvider {
+    /// Read the current secret at whatever version is stored.
+    public func get(_ reference: OpenMedSecretReference) throws -> OpenMedSecretValue {
+        try get(reference, expectedVersion: nil)
+    }
+}
diff --git a/swift/OpenMedKit/Tests/OpenMedKitTests/KeychainSecretProviderTests.swift b/swift/OpenMedKit/Tests/OpenMedKitTests/KeychainSecretProviderTests.swift
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..cb3d5d795
--- /dev/null
+++ b/swift/OpenMedKit/Tests/OpenMedKitTests/KeychainSecretProviderTests.swift
@@ -0,0 +1,752 @@
+import Foundation
+import Security
+import XCTest
+
+@testable import OpenMedKit
+
+/// In-memory stand-in for the four `SecItem` calls.
+///
+/// It matches every query attribute the way the data-protection Keychain
+/// does for generic passwords, records each call, and can simulate a locked
+/// device, an access control that no longer releases the bytes, forced
+/// statuses and a concurrent writer.
+private final class FakeKeychain: OpenMedKeychainItemClient, @unchecked Sendable {
+    struct Call {
+        let operation: String
+        let query: [String: Any]
+        let attributes: [String: Any]?
+    }
+
+    private static let defaultGroup = "fake.default-group"
+    private static let controlKeys: Set<String> = [
+        kSecClass as String,
+        kSecMatchLimit as String,
+        kSecReturnData as String,
+        kSecReturnAttributes as String,
+        kSecUseDataProtectionKeychain as String,
+        kSecValueData as String,
+    ]
+
+    private let lock = NSLock()
+    private var items: [(attributes: [String: Any], data: Data)] = []
+    private var recorded: [Call] = []
+    private var lockedDevice = false
+    private var dataUnreadable = false
+    private var forced: [String: OSStatus] = [:]
+    private var beforeUpdate: (() -> Void)?
+
+    var calls: [Call] {
+        lock.lock()
+        defer { lock.unlock() }
+        return recorded
+    }
+
+    var itemCount: Int {
+        lock.lock()
+        defer { lock.unlock() }
+        return items.count
+    }
+
+    func setLocked(_ value: Bool) {
+        lock.lock()
+        lockedDevice = value
+        lock.unlock()
+    }
+
+    func setDataUnreadable(_ value: Bool) {
+        lock.lock()
+        dataUnreadable = value
+        lock.unlock()
+    }
+
+    func force(_ operation: String, _ status: OSStatus?) {
+        lock.lock()
+        forced[operation] = status
+        lock.unlock()
+    }
+
+    func onNextUpdate(_ action: @escaping () -> Void) {
+        lock.lock()
+        beforeUpdate = action
+        lock.unlock()
+    }
+
+    /// Insert an item directly, bypassing the provider.
+    func plant(_ attributes: [String: Any], data: Data) {
+        lock.lock()
+        items.append((normalized(attributes), data))
+        lock.unlock()
+    }
+
+    /// Change one attribute of every stored item, bypassing the provider.
+    func rewrite(_ key: String, to value: Any, data: Data? = nil) {
+        lock.lock()
+        for index in items.indices {
+            items[index].attributes[key] = value
+            if let data { items[index].data = data }
+        }
+        lock.unlock()
+    }
+
+    func add(_ attributes: [String: Any]) -> OSStatus {
+        lock.lock()
+        defer { lock.unlock() }
+        recorded.append(Call(operation: "add", query: attributes, attributes: nil))
+        if let status = forced["add"] { return status }
+        if lockedDevice { return errSecInteractionNotAllowed }
+        guard let data = attributes[kSecValueData as String] as? Data else { return errSecParam }
+        let candidate = normalized(attributes)
+        let identity = [kSecAttrService, kSecAttrAccount, kSecAttrAccessGroup, kSecAttrSynchronizable].map { $0 as String }
+        if items.contains(where: { item in identity.allSatisfy { Self.equal(item.attributes[$0], candidate[$0]) } }) {
+            return errSecDuplicateItem
+        }
+        items.append((candidate, data))
+        return errSecSuccess
+    }
+
+    func copyMatching(_ query: [String: Any]) -> (status: OSStatus, result: AnyObject?) {
+        lock.lock()
+        defer { lock.unlock() }
+        recorded.append(Call(operation: "copy", query: query, attributes: nil))
+        if let status = forced["copy"] { return (status, nil) }
+        if lockedDevice { return (errSecInteractionNotAllowed, nil) }
+        guard let item = items.first(where: { matches($0.attributes, query) }) else {
+            return (errSecItemNotFound, nil)
+        }
+        let wantsData = query[kSecReturnData as String] as? Bool == true
+        if wantsData, dataUnreadable { return (errSecItemNotFound, nil) }
+        var result = item.attributes
+        if wantsData { result[kSecValueData as String] = item.data }
+        if query[kSecReturnAttributes as String] as? Bool != true { return (errSecSuccess, item.data as NSData) }
+        return (errSecSuccess, result as NSDictionary)
+    }
+
+    func update(_ query: [String: Any], attributes: [String: Any]) -> OSStatus {
+        lock.lock()
+        let hook = beforeUpdate
+        beforeUpdate = nil
+        lock.unlock()
+        hook?()
+
+        lock.lock()
+        defer { lock.unlock() }
+        recorded.append(Call(operation: "update", query: query, attributes: attributes))
+        if let status = forced["update"] { return status }
+        if lockedDevice { return errSecInteractionNotAllowed }
+        guard let index = items.firstIndex(where: { matches($0.attributes, query) }) else { return errSecItemNotFound }
+        for (key, value) in attributes where key != kSecValueData as String {
+            items[index].attributes[key] = value
+        }
+        if let data = attributes[kSecValueData as String] as? Data { items[index].data = data }
+        return errSecSuccess
+    }
+
+    func delete(_ query: [String: Any]) -> OSStatus {
+        lock.lock()
+        defer { lock.unlock() }
+        recorded.append(Call(operation: "delete", query: query, attributes: nil))
+        if let status = forced["delete"] { return status }
+        let before = items.count
+        items.removeAll { matches($0.attributes, query) }
+        return items.count == before ? errSecItemNotFound : errSecSuccess
+    }
+
+    private func normalized(_ attributes: [String: Any]) -> [String: Any] {
+        var stored = attributes
+        for key in Self.controlKeys { stored.removeValue(forKey: key) }
+        if stored[kSecAttrAccessGroup as String] == nil { stored[kSecAttrAccessGroup as String] = Self.defaultGroup }
+        if stored[kSecAttrSynchronizable as String] == nil { stored[kSecAttrSynchronizable as String] = false }
+        return stored
+    }
+
+    private func matches(_ attributes: [String: Any], _ query: [String: Any]) -> Bool {
+        query.allSatisfy { key, value in
+            Self.controlKeys.contains(key) || Self.equal(attributes[key], value)
+        }
+    }
+
+    private static func equal(_ lhs: Any?, _ rhs: Any?) -> Bool {
+        switch (lhs, rhs) {
+        case (nil, nil):
+            return true
+        case (let lhs?, let rhs?):
+            return (lhs as AnyObject).isEqual(rhs)
+        default:
+            return false
+        }
+    }
+}
+
+private struct FakeProbe: OpenMedLocalAuthenticationProbe {
+    var passcode: OpenMedProtectionAvailability = .available
+    var biometry: OpenMedProtectionAvailability = .available
+
+    func availability(of requirement: OpenMedLocalAuthenticationRequirement) -> OpenMedProtectionAvailability {
+        requirement == .devicePasscode ? passcode : biometry
+    }
+}
+
+final class KeychainSecretProviderTests: XCTestCase {
+    private static let sentinel = "OMKSENTINEL7Q4Z"
+    private static let service = "org.example.\(sentinel).service"
+    private static let group = "TEAMID.org.example.\(sentinel).shared"
+    private static let secret = Data("synthetic-\(sentinel)-key-material".utf8)
+    private static let rotatedSecret = Data("synthetic-\(sentinel)-rotated-material".utf8)
+
+    private var keychain: FakeKeychain!
+
+    override func setUp() {
+        super.setUp()
+        keychain = FakeKeychain()
+    }
+
+    private func makeProvider(
+        accessGroup: OpenMedKeychainConfiguration.AccessGroup = .applicationDefault,
+        accessibility: OpenMedKeychainConfiguration.Accessibility = .whenUnlockedThisDeviceOnly,
+        userAuthentication: OpenMedKeychainConfiguration.UserAuthentication = .notRequired,
+        probe: FakeProbe = FakeProbe()
+    ) throws -> OpenMedKeychainSecretProvider {
+        let configuration = try OpenMedKeychainConfiguration(
+            service: Self.service,
+            accessGroup: accessGroup,
+            accessibility: accessibility,
+            userAuthentication: userAuthentication
+        )
+        return OpenMedKeychainSecretProvider(configuration: configuration, client: keychain, authenticationProbe: probe)
+    }
